  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Mutare- Livelihoods Protection and Promotion Programme (Year 4)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">the purpose of theproject is to improve food and income security of 3 000 poor and most vulnerable groups in 3 wards in Nyanga District by 2012. The 3 wards chosen in Nyanga are located in natural region 4 and 5 with very sandy and poor soils in terms of fertility; these areas are in the semi-arid regions. Food insecurity was the major problem that affected the proposed wards of operation and the district in general. Some of the causes of food insecurity ranged from inadequate and unevenly distributed rains, poor soils, too much reliance on rain fed fields. Food insecurity affects all groups in the community but the most hit are the very poor and vulnerable and these include, households with high dependency ratios, the disabled, the terminally ill and the child headed households.

Output 1:  Improved food security through increased productivity and income generation.
Output 2: Improved access to clean water, sanitation and hygiene
Output 3:</narrative>
  </description>
